  "notes": "USAGE:\n{戦慄|せんりつ} is a literary and dramatic word. In everyday speech, people are more likely to say {身震|みぶる}いする (to shudder) or ぞっとする (to be horrified). {戦慄|せんりつ} appears frequently in news, literature, and dramatic contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {戦慄|せんりつ}が{走|はし}る (a shudder runs through one)\n- {戦慄|せんりつ}を{覚|おぼ}える (to feel a shudder)\n- {戦慄|せんりつ}する (to shudder, to tremble)\n- {戦慄|せんりつ}すべき (horrifying, shudder-inducing)\n\nNOTE:\nDo not confuse with the homophone {旋律|せんりつ} (melody).",
